	('9bc65bb6-d22d-47d2-ba24-735730029427',2,1454,'WAH BASIC - Hill City, SD, US | Kevin Bybee',NULL,'weekly','23740 Storm Mountain Rd','SD',NULL,'Black Hills ','57702','US',-103.3769150,43.9639760,'South Dakota',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-09-12 15:20:45','2024-09-15 15:20:45',NULL,'Wild at Heart BASIC - Black Hills 2024 is back for year four! The \"Locking Shields\" men\'s group from Rapid City, SD will be hosting this years event at the beautiful Storm Mountain Retreat Center (near Rockerville, SD).  \r\n\r\nWhat to Expect:\r\n\r\nAmple time to enjoy God\'s beauty. \r\n\r\nActivities (Optional) - Hiking, Mt. Biking, Fishing, Road Biking, Basketball, Volleyball\r\n\r\nNightly Camp Fire\r\n\r\n8 Full Meals + Snacks\r\n\r\n10 Video Sessions from the Wild at Heart Team.\r\n\r\n3 Nights Lodging\r\n\r\nSpace is limited and usually fills up quickly! $100 down secures your spot and is limited to the first 20 who register! Full payment is due by 9/1/24. Packing lists and recommendations will be emailed as the event draws near. \r\n\r\nCost is $225 per person.\r\n\r\nRegistration closes on 9/1/24. Please contact Kevin for more information.\r\n\r\nTo register follow this link:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/19Ucq0mGx-xkSFSqfzsj2fm7gwb4yewDPx5Leaj09joE/edit\r\n\r\nI look forward to locking shields with you as we look to recover our Warrior Heart!!! - \r\n\r\nKevin',15618,427864,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5363\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"23740 Storm Mountain Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"Storm Mountain Retreat Center\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Black Hills \\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"SD\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"57702\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"43.963976\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-103.376915\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"South Dakota\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-hill-city-sd-us-kevin-bybee',NULL,'2020-12-04 08:12:26','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb6-ed8e-4cd9-9e6c-367097d6b37d',2,1455,'WAH BASIC - Chichester, SXW, GB | Mark Gidney',NULL,'weekly','Cobnor Activities Centre',NULL,NULL,'Chichester','PO18 8TE','GB',-0.8782630,50.8197730,'West Sussex',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-09-05 15:20:45','2024-09-08 15:20:45',NULL,'This is our 3rd Boot Camp and is based in hostel type accommodation overlooking the water on the UK\'s south coast. We always have a fire. This a great space and ideal location for walks, mountain biking, kayaking... or quiet contemplation over the WAH sessions. Already looking forward to it!',31967,447663,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9732\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Cobnor Activities Centre\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"Chidham\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Chichester\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"SXW\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"PO18 8TE\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"gb\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"50.819773\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-0.878263\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"West Sussex\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United Kingdom\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-chichester-sxw-gb-mark-gidney',NULL,'2024-02-09 07:02:10','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-0979-40e4-bb7a-e99370c9ee00',2,1456,'WAH BASIC - Van Reenen, KN, ZA | Ilana Kloppers',NULL,'weekly','Van Reenen ,','KN',NULL,'Van Reenen','','ZA',29.3838280,-28.3753460,'KwaZulu-Natal',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-09-05 15:20:45','2024-09-08 15:20:45',NULL,'Kit List (Suggested)\r\nSleeping bag, pillow, sheet – (bed and mattress provided)\r\nEarplugs x 2 pairs. (One for you in the chalet, one for when things get loud.)\r\nHiking boots if you want to take a stroll.\r\nRunning shoes if you wish to run up the mountain.\r\nSexy old clothes – nobody to impress in the bush.\r\nRaincoat – it may get wet.\r\nJacket – cold in winter. It\'s really cold in winter.\r\nShoes\r\nSlops\r\nSwim costume – summer splash pool &amp; dam available\r\nToiletries\r\nTowel\r\nWater bottle\r\nPartridge x1\r\nHeadlamp\r\nCamp Chair\r\nWide-brimmed hat\r\nInsect repellent\r\nSunscreen\r\nWalking Stick\r\nPear tree for the Partridge\r\nFishing kit – there are bass in the dam.',31771,369075,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9493\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Van Reenen ,\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Van Reenen\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"KN\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"za\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"-28.375346\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"29.383828\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"KwaZulu-Natal\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"South Africa\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-van-reenen-kn-za-ilana-kloppers-6',NULL,'2023-12-06 12:12:32','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-259f-41e9-8e88-f63dcf6a2f46',2,1457,'WAH BASIC - Mount Dora, FL, US | Matt L',NULL,'weekly','Warren Willis Camp & Conference Center ','FL',NULL,'Fruitland Park','34731','US',-81.8676790,28.8518610,'Florida',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-08-30 15:20:45','2024-09-02 15:20:45',NULL,'Situated in a beautiful retreat center on Lake Griffin, we encourage you to bring a camp chair, a flashlight, a swimsuit, and anything else you may need to enjoy easy hiking trails alongside the lake.',31917,373648,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9670\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Warren Willis Camp & Conference Center \\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"4990 Picciola Rd\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Fruitland Park\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"FL\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"34731\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"28.851861\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-81.867679\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Florida\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-mount-dora-fl-us-matt-l',NULL,'2024-01-25 03:01:25','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-411a-4802-ba91-20b60befc135',4,1458,'BECOMING A KING RETREAT- Lake City, CO, US | Dannon Wells',NULL,'weekly','2175 HWY 149','CO',NULL,'Lake City','81235','US',-107.3012290,37.9999180,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-08-29 15:20:45','2024-09-01 15:20:45',NULL,'This event takes place in the heart of the majestic San Juan Mountains of Colorado at the rustic Legacy Lodge in Lake City, CO at 8,700ft. Surrounded by forest service land and located in the most remote county with more land above 13,000ft in the lower 48 states, it is the perfect place to unplug from the world and meet with God in the company of men around camp fires and hiking trails. \r\n\r\nAccommodations: Guest rooms sleep 5 with private baths. Pillows, sheets, and towels are provided.\r\nMeals: All meals are provided\r\nActivities on and around the property: Hiking, Biking, Fly Fishing, Frisbee Golf, and Camp Fires\r\n\r\nContact for more information and registration. Cost is $425. Scholarships are available!',32008,421809,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9776\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"2175 HWY 149\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lake City\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"81235\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"37.999918\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-107.301229\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/becoming-king-retreat-lake-city-co-us-dannon-wells',NULL,'2024-02-22 05:02:23','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-5d6a-4962-b7ea-cd3ef563008c',2,118,'WAH BASIC - Estes Park, CO, US | Gail Mclain',NULL,'weekly','515 Grand Estates Dr.','CO',NULL,'Estes Park','80517','US',-105.4955580,40.3788690,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-08-22 15:20:45','2024-08-25 15:20:45',NULL,'Definitely bring; your Bible, journal, water bottle, bath towels, and multi layers for various weather conditions in the high country. If you are traveling by air and unable to bring bulky items, such as towels please let us know and we will be glad to provide those for you.\r\nFor your free time (approx. 3 hrs.) bring; hiking gear, mountain climbing gear, mountain bikes, horse back riding and ATV rentals are also available!\r\nIdeas for free time; hiking, biking, sailing, kayaking, reading, journaling, snowshoeing... weather pending!!  However you enjoy spending alone time with Father God!\r\nMost of all, bring an open heart! We\'ll provide the rest!\r\n*If you communicate by email, please include your phone number.',32150,434550,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9931\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"515 Grand Estates Dr.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Estes Park\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80517\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"40.378869\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-105.495558\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-estes-park-co-us-gail-mclain-6',NULL,'2024-04-04 01:04:18','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-79cf-4279-bf80-6ebc76a24fae',2,1458,'WAH BASIC - Lake City, CO, US | Dannon Wells',NULL,'weekly','2175 HWY 149','CO',NULL,'Lake City','81235','US',-107.3012290,37.9999180,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-08-15 15:20:45','2024-08-18 15:20:45',NULL,'This event takes place in the heart of the majestic San Juan Mountains of Colorado at the rustic Legacy Lodge. It is located in the most remote county with more land above 13,000 ft than anywhere else in the lower 48 states.  This remote valley, located at 9,000ft elevation, is a place to unplug and meet with God in the company of men around camp fires and hiking trails.  This retreat is designed to help you recover your heart and set you on the path to becoming the man God created you to be as a man, leader, husband, and father.  We have space for 25 to 35 men, so it is the perfect place to bring a few friends.  \r\n\r\nAccommodations: Guest rooms sleep 5 with private bath. Pillows, Sheets, and towels are provided.\r\nMeals: All meals are provided\r\nActivities on and around the property: Hiking, Biking, Fly Fishing, Frisbee Golf, and Camp Fires\r\nClothing: Be prepared for temperatures in the 70\'s during the day and 30\'s at night.  \r\n\r\nContact for more information and registration. Cost is $375.  Scholarships are available!',32006,421809,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9774\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"2175 HWY 149\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lake City\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"81235\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"37.999918\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-107.301229\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-lake-city-co-us-dannon-wells',NULL,'2024-02-22 04:02:23','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-968d-47f5-91e9-234a3e41152b',3,118,'CORE - Estes Park, CO, US | Gail Mclain',NULL,'weekly','515 Grand Estates Dr.','CO',NULL,'Estes Park','80517','US',-105.4955580,40.3788690,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-08-15 15:20:45','2024-08-18 15:20:45',NULL,'Definitely bring; your Bible, journal, bath towels, slippers and multi layers for various weather conditions in the high country. If you are traveling by air and unable to bring bulky items such as towels, please let us know and we will be glad to provide those for you.\r\nFor your free time (approx. 3 hrs.) bring; hiking gear, hammock, art supplies or other hand work! You\'re most welcome to play our piano! If driving; you are welcome to bring a mountain bike or road bike, nearby rentals are also available.\r\nIdeas for free time; hiking, biking, sailing, kayaking, reading, journaling, snowshoeing... weather pending!!  However you enjoy spending alone time with Father God!\r\nMost of all, bring a warm and open heart! We\'ll provide the chocolate!\r\n*If you communicate by email, please include your phone number.',32144,434550,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9922\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"515 Grand Estates Dr.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Estes Park\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80517\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"40.378869\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-105.495558\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-estes-park-co-us-gail-mclain-10',NULL,'2024-04-04 01:04:40','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-b2d1-4bd4-96fe-bd3048322300',2,635,'WAH BASIC - Lakewood, WI, US | Chad Hendricks',NULL,'weekly','18495 PEEK RD ','WI',NULL,'Lakewood','54138','US',-88.3904630,45.3449660,'Wisconsin',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-08-08 15:20:45','2024-08-11 15:20:45',NULL,'This will be our seventh year at our location is an old 80 acre family farm in Lakewood, WI.  This land is surrounded by the Nicolet National Forest.  We will be camping outside.  You can bring a camper or tent.  It will be an amazing experience of unplugging from the modern world. \r\n\r\nStart Time: \r\n\r\nNoon to 6pm is your time to set up camp.  Dinner will start at 6pm on Thursday with our first session following.\r\n\r\nWhat Should I bring: \r\n\r\nBring a notebook/journal and pens.  Camping gear. If you need something, just ask.\r\n\r\nWatch with an alarm. Because you don\'t want to be looking at your phone.\r\n\r\nAccommodations: \r\n\r\nBring your own tents, campers and gear.  If you don\'t own any of these items, please let me know and we will find what you need.\r\n\r\nRegistration Fee:\r\n\r\nThe fees for this event is to help pay for fresh water, gasoline for the generator, snacks, toilet paper, etc. \r\n\r\nThere is an option to buy the meal plan option.  \r\n\r\nAirports:\r\n\r\nClosest airport is Austin Straubel in Green Bay, WI. (1.5 hours drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nGeneral Mitchell in Milwaukee, WI (3 hr 15 min drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nOther Activities: \r\n\r\nThere is free time each day.  Currently, we have map and compass (orienteering), archery, and airsoft (chip in for extra costs). \r\n\r\nFOOD:\r\n\r\nYou can bring your own food, but you can also purchase food with the group. If you bring food, plan on keeping preparation time to a minimum. (I recommend bringing some snacks and letting the food prep to the professionals.)  Food orders will be collected before the event via email and payment will be made when you register.  It is an amazing menu with smoked pulled port, baked french toast, burgers, kabobs, and more.  \r\n\r\nVegetarian and vegan dietary needs can be accommodated. Please share any dietary needs on the sign up form. The chefs will be in contact with you to make sure their plans fit your needs.',31499,411000,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9173\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"18495 PEEK RD \\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lakewood\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"WI\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"54138\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"45.344966\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-88.390463\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Wisconsin\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-lakewood-wi-us-chad-hendricks-4',NULL,'2023-08-23 10:08:11','2024-04-10 15:20:45'),
	('9bc65bb7-cf9f-4b5b-8f37-20d40815302c',3,118,'CORE - Estes Park, CO, US | Gail Mclain',NULL,'weekly','515 Grand Estates Dr.','CO',NULL,'Estes Park','80517','US',-105.4955580,40.3788690,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:45',0,'men','2024-07-23 15:20:46','2024-07-26 15:20:46',NULL,'Definitely bring; your Bible, journal, bath towels, slippers and multi layers for various weather conditions in the high country. If you are traveling by air and unable to bring bulky items such as towels, please let us know and we will be glad to provide those for you.\r\nFor your free time (approx. 3 hrs.) bring; hiking gear, hammock, art supplies or other hand work! You\'re most welcome to play our piano! If driving; you are welcome to bring a mountain bike or road bike, nearby rentals are also available.\r\nIdeas for free time; hiking, biking, sailing, kayaking, reading, journaling, snowshoeing... weather pending!!  However you enjoy spending alone time with Father God!\r\nMost of all, bring a warm and open heart! We\'ll provide the chocolate!\r\n*If you communicate by email, please include your phone number.',32142,434550,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9919\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"515 Grand Estates Dr.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Estes Park\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80517\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"40.378869\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-105.495558\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-estes-park-co-us-gail-mclain-9',NULL,'2024-04-04 01:04:07','2024-04-10 15:20:46'),
	('9bc65bb7-ec2b-459e-a390-4dcf498e2af7',2,118,'WAH BASIC - Estes Park, CO, US | Gail Mclain',NULL,'weekly','515 Grand Estates Dr.','CO',NULL,'Estes Park','80517','US',-105.4955580,40.3788690,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:46',0,'men','2024-07-11 15:20:46','2024-07-14 15:20:46',NULL,'Definitely bring; your Bible, journal, water bottle, bath towels, and multi layers for various weather conditions in the high country. If you are traveling by air and unable to bring bulky items, such as towels please let us know and we will be glad to provide those for you.\r\nFor your free time (approx. 3 hrs.) bring; hiking gear, mountain climbing gear, mountain bikes, horse back riding and ATV rentals are also available!\r\nIdeas for free time; hiking, biking, sailing, kayaking, reading, journaling, snowshoeing... weather pending!!  However you enjoy spending alone time with Father God!\r\nMost of all, bring an open heart! We\'ll provide the rest!\r\n*If you communicate by email, please include your phone number.',32148,434550,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9928\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"515 Grand Estates Dr.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Estes Park\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80517\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"40.378869\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-105.495558\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-estes-park-co-us-gail-mclain-5',NULL,'2024-04-04 01:04:38','2024-04-10 15:20:46'),
	('9bc65bb8-08ed-4e84-8f00-7e27b5014bb0',4,1459,'BECOMING A KING RETREAT- Colorado Springs, CO, US | Brad Steininger',NULL,'weekly','5125 Brady Rd','CO',NULL,'Colorado Springs','80915','US',-104.7319960,38.8627910,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:20:46',0,'men','2024-07-11 15:20:46','2024-07-14 15:20:46',NULL,'NOTE: Registration for this retreat is closed (we have already filled all the slots). Please email or text if you would like to be notified of future retreats (and be given first opportunity to register).\r\n\r\nWhen: Thur-Sun, July 11-14, 2024 (arrive at 5:00 pm Thursday, depart after 12:00 Sunday)\r\n\r\nWhere: The Outpost at Stein Haus, 5125 Brady Rd, Colorado Springs, CO 80915\r\n\r\nWho: It is open to men of all ages (18 and above). This retreat can accommodate up to 4 men.\r\n\r\nAccommodations: Four men will share a single large room (bunk beds). Everyone will have a bed, pillow, linens and towels. There is one bathroom with a shower/sink/toilet and a second bathroom with a sink/toilet.\r\n\r\nCost: $77 which includes lodging, all meals and retreat content. A nonrefundable deposit of $50 is due no later than eight weeks prior to the retreat via check or PayPal. Full payment of the remaining $27 is due upon arrival at the retreat.\r\n\r\nRegistration: Please contact Brad Steininger to register or to request more information.\r\n\r\nOther info:\r\n\r\n* This event is designed to be experienced \"off the grid;\" we require participants to unplug from all devices. There will be a contact number provided for emergencies.\r\n\r\n* A couple hours of free time is built into the schedule both Friday and Saturday afternoons. During this time you will have the opportunity to participate in a hike, leisure time around the facility, take a nap, read a book, etc.\r\n\r\n* This retreat is hosted in a private residence in a rustic neighborhood on the East side of Colorado Springs. Bring season-appropriate casual clothes. There are some trails nearby for hiking and an excellent park with many trails just a couple miles away.\r\n\r\n* In the evenings, there will be an opportunity to relax, build a camp fire, tell stories and have fun. You\'ll leave with new friendships, greater clarity in your walk with the Lord, and inspired to live your life as a man fully alive.',31659,236529,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9357\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"5125 Brady Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Colorado Springs\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80915\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"38.862791\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-104.731996\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/becoming-king-retreat-colorado-springs-co-us-brad-steininger-9',NULL,'2023-10-25 12:10:25','2024-04-10 15:20:46'),
