	('9bc65bda-7807-46cf-8054-3d977373996d',5,1624,'WILD AT HEART - Colorado Springs , CO, US | Ed McGaw',NULL,'weekly','Envoy Church','CO',NULL,'Colorado Springs ','80915','US',-104.7471640,38.8627330,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:08',0,'men','2023-09-27 15:21:08',NULL,NULL,'Wednesday 6:15-7:45 PM, Sep 27 thru Nov 15\r\nTo register, you will need to create a profile at EnvoyChurchCenter.com and then visit groups /  Wild at heart to enroll.  You can also contact me directly.  Books can be purchased at Amazon',31487,382463,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9160\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Envoy Church\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"2025 N Murray Blvd\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Colorado Springs \\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80915\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"38.862733\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-104.747164\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wildatheart/small-group/wild-heart-colorado-springs-co-us-ed-mcgaw',NULL,'2023-08-21 09:08:46','2024-04-10 15:21:08'),
	('9bc65bda-94dc-4c8b-b1ba-0a384e787136',6,1644,'CAPTIVATING - Colorado Springs , CO, US | Deborah Nottingham',NULL,'weekly','2025 N Murray Blvd','CO',NULL,'Colorado Springs ','80915','US',-104.7471150,38.8629760,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:08',0,'women','2023-09-27 15:21:08',NULL,NULL,'6:15-7:45 pm September 27 through November 15\r\nTo register, you will need to create a profile at Envoychurchcenter.com to register directly in the group. Visit groups /Captivating to register. You can also contact me directly. Group size limited to 10. Cost for Discussion guide is $8',31485,470403,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9158\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"2025 N Murray Blvd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"Envoy Chirch\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Colorado Springs \\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80915\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"38.862976\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-104.747115\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/captivating/small-group/captivating-colorado-springs-co-us-deborah-nottingham',NULL,'2023-08-21 09:08:19','2024-04-10 15:21:08'),
	('9bc65bda-b0fb-4481-b117-6854c90e958e',3,1645,'CORE - Schulenburg, TX, US | Andi Parris',NULL,'weekly','2123 FM 2238','TX',NULL,'Schulenburg','78956','US',-96.9030370,29.6819000,'Texas',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:08',0,'men','2023-08-18 15:21:08','2023-08-21 15:21:08',NULL,'The Captivating retreat will be hosted at the beautiful Camp Jordan. This retreat center is hotel style with bedding, towels, and pillows provided. \r\n\r\nWhen you are gathering items to bring in your bag, pack like you would for a hotel.\r\nThere will be opportunities to spend time outside to explore the 80+ acres of property. We will have access to the swimming pool and hot tub. Bring shoes safe to walk in, and your swimsuit if you want to enjoy the water.\r\n\r\nArrival time: Friday, August 18th @ 1pm\r\nDeparture time: Sunday, August 20th @1pm\r\n\r\nCorrect Address: \r\n2123 FM 2238\r\nSchulenburg, TX 78956\r\n\r\nRoom Info:\r\n\r\nThe rooms sleep 3 people.  Each room has a bathroom and hotel style bedding and beds. \r\n\r\nRoom assignments will be provided upon check.  The retreat has a hotel check in desk and will give you a room key upon check in.\r\n\r\nSuggested items for a comfortable stay:\r\n\r\n•Toothbrush and toothpaste\r\n•Deodorant\r\n•Hair brush\r\n•Sunscreen\r\n•Shampoo/Conditioner and body wash\r\n•Makeup/hair care products if desired\r\n•Any medication, or supplements you take daily \r\n\r\n•3-4 outfits\r\n•Light jacket or blanket for indoor conference time\r\n•Undergarments\r\n•Socks\r\n•Sandals and/or shoes safe for walking\r\n•Swimsuit\r\n\r\n\r\n•Bible &amp; pen\r\n•Tumbler for water or coffee\r\n•Speaker for your room, ear plugs or sound machine',31269,449984,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8922\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"2123 FM 2238\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Schulenburg\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"TX\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"78956\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"29.681900\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-96.903037\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Texas\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-schulenburg-tx-us-andi-parris',NULL,'2023-06-13 07:06:27','2024-04-10 15:21:08'),
	('9bc65bda-cd7d-4dd2-9850-1bf7cd45d6a4',2,1646,'WAH BASIC - Boca Raton, FL, US | Timothy Frank',NULL,'weekly','11387 Nacoma Way','FL',NULL,'Boca Raton','33428-1129','US',-80.2254000,26.3629460,'Florida',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:08',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:08','2023-08-20 15:21:08',NULL,'',31385,231158,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9041\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"11387 Nacoma Way\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Boca Raton\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"FL\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"33428-1129\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"26.362946\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-80.225400\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Florida\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-boca-raton-fl-us-timothy-frank',NULL,'2023-07-22 08:07:57','2024-04-10 15:21:08'),
	('9bc65bda-ebcf-4b39-8556-2b61080c4433',2,635,'WAH BASIC - Lakewood, WI, US | Chad Hendricks',NULL,'weekly','18495 PEEK RD','WI',NULL,'Lakewood','54138','US',-88.3904800,45.3449970,'Wisconsin',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:08',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:09','2023-08-20 15:21:09',NULL,'Location: \r\n\r\nOur location is an old 80 acre family farm in Lakewood, WI.  This land is surrounded by the Nicolet National Forest.  We will be camping outside with no running water or electricity.  It will be an amazing experience of unplugging from the modern world. \r\n\r\nStart Time: \r\n\r\nNoon to 6pm is your time to set up camp.  Dinner will start at 6pm on Thursday with our first session following.\r\n\r\nWhat Should I bring: \r\n\r\nBring a notebook/journal and pens.  Camping gear. If you need something, just ask.\r\n\r\nWatch with an alarm. Because you don\'t want to be looking at your phone.\r\n\r\nAccommodations: \r\n\r\nBring your own tents, campers and gear.  If you don\'t own any of these items, please let me know and we will find what you need.\r\n\r\nRegistration Fee: $25 and $125 more for the food plan. \r\n\r\nThe fees for this event is to help pay for fresh water, gasoline for the generator, snacks, toilet paper, etc. \r\n\r\nThere is an option to buy the meal plan option.  We will be having a local restaurant cater to us. \r\n\r\nAirports:\r\n\r\nClosest airport is Austin Straubel in Green Bay, WI. (1.5 hours drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nGeneral Mitchell in Milwaukee, WI (3 hr 15 min drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nOther Activities: \r\n\r\nThere is free time each day.  Currently, we will be offering  map and compass (orienteering) training and archery training as added activities. \r\n\r\nFOOD:\r\n\r\nYou can bring your own food, but you can also purchase food with the group. If you bring food, plan on keeping preparation time to a minimum. (I recommend bringing some snacks and letting the food prep to the professionals.)  Food orders will be collected before the event via email and payment will be made when you register.  The menu for this trip is below. \r\n\r\nTotal Food Costs: $105.00 plus $20 for tip\r\n\r\nBreakfast @ $10 each (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)1. Scrambled Eggs, Sausage, Tator tots, English muffin, Danish2. Ham &amp; Egg on an English muffin, hashbrowns, yogurt, mixed fruit3. Pancakes &amp; Syrup, sausage links, American fries, apple,\r\n\r\nLunch @ $10 each (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)1. Chicken Bacon Wrap, granola bar, chips2. sub sandwich, cookie, chips3. Burger with potato wedges\r\n\r\nDinner @ $15 each (Thursday, Friday, Saturday)1. 3 piece Broasted chicken, mashed potatoes, dressing, Green Beans, Pasta Salad2. 1/2 Rack BBQ ribs, baked potato, dinner roll, side salad3. Fish Fry (Friday) Breaded Alaskan Pollack , baby reds, coleslaw, rye bread',17787,411000,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"7495\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"18495 PEEK RD\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lakewood\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"WI\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"54138\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"45.344997\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-88.390480\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Wisconsin\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-lakewood-wi-us-chad-hendricks-3',NULL,'2022-08-22 07:08:54','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-0929-4c40-be11-713d91597e53',2,1469,'WAH BASIC - Effie, MN, US | Skip Johnson',NULL,'weekly','65328 County Road 235','MN',NULL,'Effie','56639','US',-93.5290540,47.8314650,'Minnesota',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:09','2023-08-20 15:21:09',NULL,'For more details, please view our sign-up link.\r\n\r\nThe weekend will be hosted at the Historic Riverbend Farm in Effie, MN, on the Bigfork River. ~4-hour drive from the Minneapolis area\r\n\r\nThe location is rustic and off the beaten path, with several hundred acres to explore. \r\n\r\nSessions are held in the beautifully restored barn. A house, two cabins, a yurt, and multiple RVs will be accommodations. It\'s a beautiful and wild location in northern MN, and if you are interested in sleeping under the stars, feel free to bring a tent.\r\n\r\nMiles of ATV trails and a river run through the property, so pack accordingly to be outside in northern MN weather. \r\n\r\nOutside of appropriate clothing, some other ideas are:\r\n\r\n-ATV or SXS if you have one\r\n-Kayak or canoe for the river\r\n-Guns and Ammo for target shooting or trap\r\n-fishing gear (muskies, northern pike, smallmouth bass, and walleyes)\r\n-Sleeping bag &amp; pillow\r\n-water shoes for the river\r\n-Bug/tick spray\r\n-Bible\r\n-Flashlight/headlamp\r\n-Folding chair or camp chair\r\n-Journal and pen',31127,430547,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8775\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"65328 County Road 235\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Effie\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"MN\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"56639\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"47.831465\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-93.529054\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Minnesota\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-effie-mn-us-skip-johnson-2',NULL,'2023-05-15 10:05:18','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-2696-4573-b118-a232c7185f1d',3,1647,'CORE - North Richland Hills, TX, US | Tonya Chapman',NULL,'weekly','7618 Woodhaven Drive','TX',NULL,'North Richland Hills','76182','US',-97.2150450,32.8896590,'Texas',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:09','2023-08-20 15:21:09',NULL,'',31212,435902,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8855\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"7618 Woodhaven Drive\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"North Richland Hills\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"TX\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"76182\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"32.889659\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-97.215045\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Texas\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-north-richland-hills-tx-us-tonya-chapman',NULL,'2023-06-04 12:06:33','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-4299-42c6-baa5-fd29b19b55a2',3,1648,'CORE - Charleston, SC, US | Tara Dalles',NULL,'weekly','0 Ripley Point Dr','SC',NULL,'Charleston','29407','US',-79.9669320,32.7770890,'South Carolina',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:09','2023-08-20 15:21:09',NULL,'',31154,465811,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8801\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"0 Ripley Point Dr\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Charleston\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"SC\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"29407\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"32.777089\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-79.966932\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"South Carolina\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-charleston-sc-us-tara-dalles',NULL,'2023-05-22 03:05:40','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-5f32-41ef-b2a2-748d23e5e1dd',3,118,'CORE - Estes Park, CO, US | Gail Mclain',NULL,'weekly','515 Grand Estates Dr.','CO',NULL,'Estes Park','80517','US',-105.4955580,40.3788690,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:09','2023-08-20 15:21:09',NULL,'Definitely bring; your Bible, journal, water bottle, bath towels, slippers and multi layers for various weather conditions in the high country. If you are traveling by air and unable to bring bulky items, please let us know and we will be glad to provide those for you.\r\n\r\nFor your free time (approx. 3 hrs.) bring; hiking gear, hammock, art supplies or other hand work! You\'re most welcome to play our piano! If driving; you are welcome to bring a mountain bike or road bike, nearby rentals are also available.\r\n\r\nIdeas for free time; hiking, biking, sailing, kayaking, reading, journaling, snowshoeing... However you enjoy spending alone time with God!\r\n\r\nMost of all, bring a warm and open heart! We\'ll provide the chocolate!\r\n\r\n*When inquiring by email, please include your phone number.',31064,434550,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8713\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"515 Grand Estates Dr.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Estes Park\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80517\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"40.378869\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-105.495558\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-estes-park-co-us-gail-mclain-5',NULL,'2023-05-01 08:05:37','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-7b88-4393-9b63-665511bd77c2',2,1649,'WAH BASIC - Copperhill, TN, US | Jake Dowling',NULL,'weekly','703 Golf Course Rd.','TN',NULL,'Copperhill','37317','US',-84.3254440,35.0349270,'Tennessee',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-08-17 15:21:09','2023-08-20 15:21:09',NULL,'When: Thurs-Sun, August 17-20, 2023 (arrive between 3:30pm and 5:00pm Thursday, depart after 12:30 Sunday)\r\n\r\nWhere: Whitewater Express Retreat Center\r\nhttps://ocoee.whitewaterexpress.com/\r\n\r\nClosest airports:  Atlanta (Approx 2.5 hours with traffic); Chattanooga (Less than 1.5 hours); Knoxville (Less than 2 hours)\r\n\r\nAccommodations: Overnight lodging will be in cabins, bunk style. All cabins have electricity and air conditioning and provide a rustic yet comfortable experience. There is a restroom and shower inside each cabin, with additional restrooms and showers in bathhouses throughout the camp. For those who like to sleep outdoors, optional “outdoor bunks” are available on the screened-in back porches of the cabins. You can request a roommate, otherwise roommates will be assigned.\r\n\r\nCost: $225, includes lodging, all meals, camp activities, and retreat content.\r\n\r\nWe will be spending the weekend on 500 acres tucked into the rolling hills of East Tennessee, near the Georgia/Tennessee border. Free time is built into the retreat on Friday and Saturday afternoons. On-site and nearby activities are available including hiking, swimming, fishing, river tubing, etc. An optional adventure activity is also included (whitewater rafting, horseback riding, or paintball). You may want to bring a hammock and find a quiet spot by a stream to rest and soak in God’s beauty. In the evenings we will have a campfire. \r\n\r\nThis event is best experienced off the grid, and we ask that you plan to arrive ready to unplug for the weekend. We promise you won’t regret it, and your texts and e-mails will still be there on Sunday afternoon.\r\n\r\nFor more information, contact:\r\nJake Dowling (jacob.d.dowling@delta.com);\r\nBeau Hughes (bbhughes8664@gmail.com); or\r\nJason Grooms (jason@absoluteclimatecontrol.com)\r\n\r\nA deposit of $100 will hold your spot. Full payment will be due by August 3rd. Payment details are included in the registration form.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re ready to register, please click here: https://forms.gle/86AwpPZyGW3DxQmd8',19710,419062,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8571\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"703 Golf Course Rd.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Copperhill\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"TN\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"37317\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"35.034927\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-84.325444\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Tennessee\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-copperhill-tn-us-jake-dowling',NULL,'2023-04-06 08:04:14','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-9986-4f10-8e41-71ab1afbba26',2,1650,'WAH BASIC - Keystone Heights, FL, US | Joshua and Melissa Sizemore',NULL,'weekly','6779 Camp Road','FL',NULL,'Keystone Heights','32656','US',-81.9379120,29.8167480,'Florida',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-08-16 15:21:09','2023-08-19 15:21:09',NULL,'This event is at a 90 acer campsite in Northeast Florida on a lake. Cost is $300 which includes food, lodging, and most events. \r\nFree time events will include, Shooting Range, Archery, Disc Golf, Swimming, Kayaking, Zipline, Scream Swing, Water Slide, Camp fires and more. If you will be shooting you will need to bring your own gun, ammo, and targets. We will have a safety ranger on site for safety at set times. Bring swimsuit, towel, Pillow, Sheets, blanket, Bathroom stuff. All meals are included. Bring Cash for any snacks that may be optional. \r\nStep 1 Email me that you are signing up: Joshua.Sizemore@c12forums.com\r\nStep 2 Send Payment via Venmo now. https://venmo.com/u/Joshua-Sizemore21\r\nStep 3 I will send you a link for you to register for the event and have paid',18931,335814,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"8488\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"6779 Camp Road\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Keystone Heights\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"FL\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"32656\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"29.816748\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-81.937912\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Florida\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-keystone-heights-fl-us-joshua-and-melissa-sizemore',NULL,'2023-03-17 08:03:52','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
	('9bc65bdb-b663-465c-a482-d6483afed1a3',5,76,'WILD AT HEART - Jacksonville, FL, US | Ed Murphy',NULL,'weekly','LOSCO REGIONAL PARK','FL',NULL,'Jacksonville','32257','US',-81.5667910,30.1779460,'Florida',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:09',0,'men','2023-09-12 15:21:09',NULL,NULL,'The Wild at Heart EXPERIENCE is a six-session study. Our format is an OUTDOOR IN-PERSON study held monthly on the second Tuesday starting September 12. You may click on the link to register. The registration link contains directions to the site, links to purchase the book, study guide and if desired the Field Manual. If you would like to work through the Field Manual with a trusted guide, contact Ed Murphy\r\nWe hope to see you there! \r\n\r\nREGISTRATION IS OPEN!\r\nhttps://mailchi.mp/5343aecc4325/2yfkteupwb',31470,236318,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"9141\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"LOSCO REGIONAL PARK\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"10932 Hood Rd.\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Jacksonville\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"FL\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"32257\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"30.177946\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-81.566791\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Florida\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wildatheart/small-group/wild-heart-jacksonville-fl-us-ed-murphy',NULL,'2023-08-16 06:08:53','2024-04-10 15:21:09'),
