	('9bc65c16-c428-495d-89f2-cb68fb3ea26e',2,1659,'WAH BASIC - Tarbert, AGB, GB | Derek Moir',NULL,'weekly','Port Ban Holiday Park',NULL,NULL,'Tarbert','PA296YD','GB',-5.6607910,55.8280460,'Argyll and Bute',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:48',0,'men','2021-10-04 15:21:48','2021-10-07 15:21:48',NULL,'There\'s facilities and equipment to kayak, mountain bike, walk and play other sports like football, volleyball. So, if you\'d like to join us bring appropriate clothing.',16387,394962,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6112\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Port Ban Holiday Park\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Tarbert\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"AGB\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"PA296YD\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"gb\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"55.828046\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-5.660791\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Argyll and Bute\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United Kingdom\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-tarbert-agb-gb-derek-moir',NULL,'2021-07-28 05:07:54','2024-04-10 15:21:48'),
	('9bc65c16-e263-4f58-b598-005a3421be71',5,1902,'WILD AT HEART - Tulsa , OK, US | Jackey Davis',NULL,'weekly','7570 w canyon rd ','OK',NULL,'Tulsa ','74131','US',-96.0767810,36.0310780,'Oklahoma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:48',0,'men','2021-10-05 15:21:48',NULL,NULL,'Meeting every other Tuesday at 6 pm.',16665,405856,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6403\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"7570 w canyon rd \\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Tulsa \\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"OK\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"74131\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"36.031078\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-96.076781\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Oklahoma\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wildatheart/small-group/wild-heart-tulsa-ok-us-jackey-davis',NULL,'2021-10-03 07:10:30','2024-04-10 15:21:48'),
	('9bc65c16-ffab-466d-a334-759baf0d6d80',2,1903,'WAH BASIC - Robert Lee, TX, US | Logan Gilbert',NULL,'weekly','400 Skyline Drive','TX',NULL,'Robert Lee','76945','US',-100.7097870,31.8126310,'Texas',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:48',0,'men','2021-09-30 15:21:48','2021-10-03 15:21:48',NULL,'Additional Information for this BASIC\r\nAnytime Acres is a privately owned homestead in a small country subdivision in Coke County, Texas. The property is located just West of Robert Lee, Texas (the county seat) where the landscape begins to transition from the sandy red desert out West to the humid greenery further Southeast. The property is a 5 minute walk to where the Colorado River feeds into E.V. Spence Reservoir. We are 1.5hrs from Midland, TX and 45 minutes from San Angelo, TX.\r\n\r\nThis location is remote and fairly minimalistic. There will be running water, restroom facilities and a shower available however this is a camping event. Each man is responsible for his own tent/sleeping arrangement. The ground is very hard so we would advise additional bedding. While I don’t want to over sell the ruggedness of this experience I do want to set the expectation of being outside in nature for several days. The ruggedness of the terrain allows you to see Gods love in different ways through his creation.\r\n\r\n There are countless options to spread out and be alone with God during our breakout sessions. If you feel like being active, play some disc golf on the mini course, relax in the swimming hole down by the lake, or go for a hike and explore. Bring your own fishing gear or kayak as there are multiple places to fish alone, from the banks or put in to the lake from the Paint Creek Dock/Ramp which is 12 minutes away. Either way during your time you should see all kinds of wildlife and be able to appreciate the quiet country life. At night, the West Texas Sky will amaze you. \r\n\r\nA Wild at Heart Basic Event allowed me to see God in a different way. At that event, I felt led to put on an event of my own; because I saw how God worked with so many men in our group during such a short time. It was awesome! Our fellowship is comprised of a small group of family and friends who love Jesus and want to see His Kingdom advance. We believe the Wild at Heart approach to building strong men who love Jesus is the exact model that Jesus himself used to impact the hearts of his followers and make disciples. It is our privilege and duty to host Wild at Heart Basic camps.\r\nFull meals of sandwiches or better equivalent will be provided Thursday evening dinner through Sunday breakfast. There will be snacks provided between sessions but you are welcome to bring any snacks, drinks or food you want. A refrigerator is available. Please let us know if you have any food allergies in advance. \r\nCheck-In: 5:00-6:30 pm on Thursday, September 30, 2021\r\nConclusion: 12:00 noon on Sunday, October 3, 2021\r\n\r\nThe total cost of the camp is $175 (with a $50 nonrefundable deposit, due at sign up). Your registration fee covers your meals and all of the teaching (video sessions) and materials by Wild at Heart for the duration of the weekend. Additional recreational supplies such as mountain bikes and fishing gear, etc. are not included. Participants must bring their own towels, shower supplies, and any additional personal items (rain gear, hiking boots, tennis shoes, etc.). Enrollment is limited, so please act quickly if you want to be a part of this camp.\r\nAdditionally, a shuttle service is available for those traveling to and from the airport in San Angelo for $75 round-trip. Pick up in Midland or Abilene can be arranged with enough notice.\r\nNeither a mask nor a vaccine is required for this event. We will not be testing any participant for Covid. If you feel ill prior to your arrival please reschedule your event. \r\nWild at Heart Basic camps are truly life changing experiences. You\'ll leave with new friendships, greater clarity about yourself, and more importantly a rediscovery of your \"wild heart\", as you connect with your Father who created it. You have permission to be yourself. You have permission to relax. You have permission to connect. Do not make any agreements with the enemy before or during the event. \r\n\r\nA battle to fight, an adventure to live, and beauty to rescue. We are all Wild at Heart!\r\n\r\nAlso, please feel free to contact Logan via text at 432-296-2544 or email at loganwgilbert@gmail.com with any further questions. See y\'all there!',16442,424889,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6157\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"400 Skyline Drive\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Robert Lee\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"TX\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"76945\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"31.812631\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-100.709787\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Texas\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-robert-lee-tx-us-logan-gilbert',NULL,'2021-08-16 08:08:13','2024-04-10 15:21:48'),
