	('9bc65c1a-ee19-473d-9421-816044de1ec7',3,1632,'CORE - Libby, MT, US | Barbara Soucy',NULL,'weekly','88 Pinecrest Drive','MT',NULL,'Libby','59923','US',-115.5795920,48.3769200,'Montana',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:50',0,'men','2021-08-19 15:21:50','2021-08-22 15:21:50',NULL,'',16434,427313,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6146\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"88 Pinecrest Drive\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Libby\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"MT\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"59923\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"48.376920\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-115.579592\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Montana\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-libby-mt-us-barbara-soucy-0',NULL,'2021-08-12 03:08:29','2024-04-10 15:21:50'),
	('9bc65c1b-0d52-4a7c-84ea-318b713420b7',2,1459,'WAH BASIC - Colorado Springs, CO, US | Brad Steininger',NULL,'weekly','5125 Brady Rd','CO',NULL,'Colorado Springs','80915','US',-104.7319960,38.8627910,'Colorado',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:50',0,'men','2021-08-19 15:21:51','2021-08-22 15:21:51',NULL,'What: This is no ordinary men\'s retreat. No breakout sessions or small groups. Just awesome teaching by John and his team via video followed by time alone with the Father.\r\n\r\nWhen: Thur-Sun, August 19-22, 2021 (arrive between 4:30-5:00 pm Thursday, depart after 12:00 Sunday)\r\n\r\nWhere: The Outpost at Stein Haus, 5125 Brady Rd, Colorado Springs, CO 80915\r\n\r\nWho: This retreat can accommodate up to 4 men (there will be a waiting list in the event someone needs to dropout).\r\n\r\nAccommodations: Four men will share a single large room (bunk beds). Everyone will have a bed, pillow, linens and towels. There is one bathroom with a shower/sink/toilet and a second bathroom with a sink/toilet.\r\n\r\nCost: $77 which includes lodging, all meals and retreat content. A nonrefundable deposit of $50 is due 5 August via check or PayPal. Full payment of the remaining $27 is due upon arrival at the retreat.\r\n\r\nRegistration: Please contact Brad Steininger to register or for more information.\r\n\r\nOther info:   \r\n\r\n* Get a copy of Wild at Heart and read it before the retreat.\r\n\r\n* This event is designed to be experienced \"off the grid;\" we ask that you unplug and only use cell phones in extreme emergencies. There will be a contact number for emergencies.\r\n\r\n* Free time is built into the schedule both Friday and Saturday afternoon. During this time you will have the opportunity to participate in a hike, leisure time around the facility, take a nap, read a book, play disc golf, etc.\r\n\r\n* This retreat is in a rustic neighborhood on the East side of Colorado Springs (mostly dirt roads and equestrian properties). Bring season-appropriate casual clothes. There are some trails nearby for hiking and an excellent park with many trails just a couple miles away. \r\n\r\n* In the evenings, there will be an opportunity to relax, build a camp fire, tell stories and have fun. You\'ll leave with new friendships, greater clarity in your walk with the Lord, and inspired to live your life as a man fully alive.',16141,236529,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5866\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"5125 Brady Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Colorado Springs\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CO\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"80915\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"38.862791\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-104.731996\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Colorado\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-colorado-springs-co-us-brad-steininger-2',NULL,'2021-04-29 03:04:45','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-2ace-4b18-a534-19081474f9f5',2,635,'WAH BASIC - Lakewood, WI, US | Chad Hendricks',NULL,'weekly','18495 PEEK RD','WI',NULL,'Lakewood','54138','US',-88.3904800,45.3449970,'Wisconsin',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-19 15:21:51','2021-08-22 15:21:51',NULL,'Our location is an old 80 acre family farm in Lakewood, WI.  This land is surrounded by the Nicolet National Forest.  We will be camping outside with no running water or electricity.  It will be an amazing experience of unplugging from the modern world. \r\n\r\nStart Time: \r\n\r\nNoon to 6pm is your time to set up camp.  Dinner will start at 6pm on Thursday with our first session following.\r\n\r\nWhat Should I bring: \r\n\r\nBring a notebook/journal and pens.  Camping gear. If you need something, just ask.\r\n\r\nAccommodations: \r\n\r\nBring your own tents, campers and gear.  If you don\'t own any of these items, please let me know and we will find what you need.\r\n\r\nRegistration Fee: $25\r\n\r\nThe fees for this event is to help pay for fresh water, gasoline for the generator, snacks, toilet paper, etc. \r\n\r\nThere is an option to buy the meal plan option.  We will be having a local restaurant cater to us. \r\n\r\nAirports:\r\n\r\nClosest airport is Austin Straubel in Green Bay, WI. (1.5 hours drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nGeneral Mitchell in Milwaukee, WI (3 hr 15 min drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nOther Activities: \r\n\r\nThere is free time each day.  Currently, we will be offering  map and compass (orienteering) training and archery training as added activities. \r\n\r\nFOOD:\r\n\r\nYou can bring your own food, but you can also purchase food with the group. If you bring food, plan on keeping preparation time to a minimum. (I recommend bringing some snacks and letting the food prep to the professionals.)  Food orders will be collected before the event via email and payment will be made when you register.  The menu for this trip is below. \r\n\r\nTotal Food Costs: $105.00 plus $20 for tip\r\n\r\nBreakfast @ $10 each (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)1. Scrambled Eggs, Sausage, Tator tots, English muffin, Danish2. Ham &amp; Egg on an English muffin, hashbrowns, yogurt, mixed fruit3. Pancakes &amp; Syrup, sausage links, American fries, apple,\r\n\r\nLunch @ $10 each (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)1. Chicken Bacon Wrap, granola bar, chips2. sub sandwich, cookie, chips3. Burger with potato wedges\r\n\r\nDinner @ $15 each (Thursday, Friday, Saturday)1. 3 piece Broasted chicken, mashed potatoes, dressing, Green Beans, Pasta Salad2. 1/2 Rack BBQ ribs, baked potato, dinner roll, side salad3. Fish Fry (Friday) Breaded Alaskan Pollack , baby reds, coleslaw, rye bread',16055,411000,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5788\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"18495 PEEK RD\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lakewood\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"WI\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"54138\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"45.344997\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-88.390480\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Wisconsin\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-lakewood-wi-us-chad-hendricks-1',NULL,'2021-04-06 01:04:50','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-4928-4a73-82e7-27333402b8f7',2,1919,'WAH BASIC - Glen, MT, US | Russ  Case',NULL,'weekly','Two Moose Camp','MT',NULL,'Glen','59732','US',-112.6892000,45.4889920,'Montana',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-19 15:21:51','2021-08-22 15:21:51',NULL,'What: This is no ordinary men\'s retreat. No breakout sessions or small groups. Just awesome teaching by John and his team via video followed by time alone with the Father.\r\n\r\nWhen: Thur-Sun, August 19-22, 2021 (arrive between 4:30-5:00 pm Thursday, depart after 12:00 Sunday)\r\n\r\nWhere: Two Moose Camp, Glen Montana\r\n\r\nWho: This retreat can accommodate up to 32 men (there will be a waiting list in the event someone needs to dropout).\r\n\r\nAccommodations: Bunkhouse, bring sleeping bag pillow, shower kit and towel\r\n\r\nCost: $200 which includes lodging, all meals and retreat content.\r\n\r\nRegistration: Please contact Russ Case russcase7@yahoo.com, call or text 405 757-5381 or Nic Larson nr.larson0107@gmail.com, call or text 605 924-0520 to register or for more information.\r\n\r\nOther info:\r\n\r\n* Get a copy of Wild at Heart and read it before the retreat.\r\n\r\n* This event is designed to be experienced \"off the grid;\" we ask that you unplug and only use cell phones in extreme emergencies. There will be a contact number for emergencies.\r\n\r\n* Free time is built into the schedule both Friday and Saturday afternoon. During this time you will have the opportunity to enjoy Montana\'s finest fishing, this camp is located on the Big Hole river, you can also participate in a hike, leisure time around the facility, take a nap, read book, etc.\r\n\r\n* This retreat is in beautiful western Montana (mostly dirt roads). Bring season-appropriate casual clothes. There are some trails nearby for hiking and an excellent fly fishing within walking distance.\r\n\r\n* Bottled water will be provided. Bring any specific snacks that you like. \r\n\r\n* In the evenings, there will be an opportunity to relax, build a camp fire, tell stories and have fun. You\'ll leave with new friendships, greater clarity in your walk with the Lord, and inspired to live your life as a man fully alive.',16225,232931,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5950\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Two Moose Camp\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Glen\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"MT\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"59732\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"45.488992\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-112.689200\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Montana\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-glen-mt-us-russ-case',NULL,'2021-05-29 05:05:23','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-66e5-4b7a-8d0e-ce97fca5b5a2',5,1914,'WILD AT HEART - Southern Pines, NC, US | Steven Myer',NULL,'weekly','Christ Community Church','NC',NULL,'Southern Pines','28387','US',-79.4490880,35.2301980,'North Carolina',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-09-25 15:21:51',NULL,NULL,'',16456,411164,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6172\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Christ Community Church\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Southern Pines\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"NC\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"28387\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"35.230198\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-79.449088\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"North Carolina\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wildatheart/small-group/wild-heart-southern-pines-nc-us-steven-myer',NULL,'2021-08-18 08:08:36','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-8537-4ec1-9c85-0d990522c3eb',3,1473,'CORE - Effie , MN, US | Skip Johnson ',NULL,'weekly','65328 County Road C E ','MN',NULL,'Effie ','56639','US',-93.5311220,47.8295210,'Minnesota',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-12 15:21:51','2021-08-15 15:21:51',NULL,'There will be free time to enjoy all that northern Minnesota has to offer! I would pack a swimsuit for the sauna and to jump in the river. Comfortable clothes for going berry picking and four wheeling. There are also canoes and kayaks to use.',16338,432639,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6065\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"65328 County Road C E \\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Effie \\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"MN\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"56639\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"47.829521\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-93.531122\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Minnesota\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-effie-mn-us-skip-johnson',NULL,'2021-07-09 02:07:29','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-a2ea-462b-bf05-7c04ab2825f0',3,1474,'CORE - George, IA, US | Wanda Van Otterloo',NULL,'weekly','2445 Jackson Ave','IA',NULL,'George','51237','US',-96.0597670,43.2979240,'Iowa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-12 15:21:51','2021-08-15 15:21:51',NULL,'This event will take place on our farm, Starting at 5:00 pm.Please bring along your swim suit, and older walking shoes . Bedding and towels will be provided. We are asking for $150.00/attendee to cover expenses. If unable to pay, contact us, we have people who are willing to help with scholarships.',16330,438752,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"6055\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"2445 Jackson Ave\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"George\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"IA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"51237\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"43.297924\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-96.059767\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Iowa\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-george-ia-us-wanda-van-otterloo',NULL,'2021-07-08 09:07:20','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-c125-4460-aebe-99d81efcfcf2',2,1920,'WAH BASIC - Palomar Mountain, CA, US |  ',NULL,'weekly','34764 Doane Valley Rd  ','CA',NULL,'Palomar Mountain','92060','US',-116.9183860,33.3466540,'California',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-12 15:21:51','2021-08-15 15:21:51',NULL,'Campfire clothes, hiking stuff',15889,434402,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5618\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"34764 Doane Valley Rd  \\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Palomar Mountain\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"92060\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"33.346654\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-116.918386\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"California\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-palomar-mountain-ca-us',NULL,'2021-03-02 05:03:14','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-ddb6-44f6-816b-870dc1a9ba74',2,1649,'WAH BASIC - Cleveland, GA, US | Jake Dowling',NULL,'weekly','1242 Old Blue Creek Rd','GA',NULL,'Cleveland','30528','US',-83.7453380,34.6063620,'Georgia',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-12 15:21:51','2021-08-15 15:21:51',NULL,'When: Thurs-Sun, August 12-15, 2021 (arrive between 3:30pm and 5pm Thursday, depart after 12:30 Sunday)\r\n\r\nWhere: The Lodge at Woodlands Camp, Cleveland GA: https://www.woodlandscamp.org/lodge-woodlands\r\n\r\nAccommodations: Lodging will be double occupancy. Each room has two queen beds. You can request a roommate, otherwise roommates will be assigned.\r\n\r\nWho: Men ages 18 and older.  \r\n\r\nCost: $250, includes lodging, all meals, and retreat content.\r\n\r\nOn-site and off-site activities will be available during free time including hiking, swimming, kayaking, etc.\r\n\r\nFor more information, contact:\r\nJake Dowling (jacob.d.dowling@delta.com);\r\nBeau Hughes (bbhughes8664@gmail.com); or \r\nMark Fischer (da.fischers@gmail.com)\r\n\r\nA deposit of $100 will be required to hold your spot. Full payment will be due by August 1st. Payment details are included in the registration form.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re ready to register, please click here:  https://forms.gle/eReRxHkmWC9Zsyid9',16110,419062,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5836\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"1242 Old Blue Creek Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Cleveland\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"GA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"30528\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"34.606362\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-83.745338\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Georgia\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-cleveland-ga-us-jake-dowling-0',NULL,'2021-04-20 08:04:21','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
	('9bc65c1b-fafd-40be-ad74-d93b78b7c5a2',2,1453,'WAH BASIC - Black Mountain, NC, US | Matthew Daughtry-Grubbs',NULL,'weekly','1233 N Fork Rd','NC',NULL,'Black Mountain','28711','US',-82.3543470,35.6253710,'North Carolina',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:21:51',0,'men','2021-08-12 15:21:51','2021-08-15 15:21:51',NULL,'Arrangements:\r\n     • Lodging will be single occupancy.  Bed linens and towels will be provided. \r\n\r\nWhat to Expect:\r\n     • Once your initial registration and payment are submitted, a welcome email will be send to you containing further details and a registration form where you will submit other information needed for the event.  \r\n     • This event is designed to be experienced \"off the grid;\" we ask that you unplug and only use cell phones in extreme emergencies, and do not carry them around the whole weekend. (There will be a contact number for emergencies.)  Further information will be provided at the event. \r\n     • Free time is built into the schedule both Friday and Saturday afternoon.  During this time you will have the opportunity to participate in a hike, enjoy the gymnasium facilities (basketball, etc.), outdoor volleyball court, leisure time around the camp grounds, or take a nap. \r\n     • In the evenings, weather permitting, we will have a camp fire. This will be a great time to relax, tell stories, and have fun. You\'ll leave with new friendships, greater clarity in your walk with the Lord, and inspired to live your life to the fullest as a man fully alive.  Please bring clothes appropriate for the weather. \r\n\r\nGroups are welcome. On the sign-up sheet sent in the welcome email, please specify what group you\'re a part of.',16150,415441,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5876\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"1233 N Fork Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Black Mountain\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"NC\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"28711\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"35.625371\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-82.354347\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"North Carolina\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-black-mountain-nc-us-matthew-daughtry-grubbs-2',NULL,'2021-05-04 08:05:24','2024-04-10 15:21:51'),
