	('9bc65c2e-c614-4734-9f7b-a87c1df5131d',2,744,'WAH BASIC - Catalina Island, Two Harbors Campground, CA, US | Andrew Hobbs',NULL,'weekly','','CA',NULL,'Catalina Island, Two Harbors Campground','90704','US',-118.4917820,33.4401890,'California',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:03',0,'men','2020-10-19 15:22:03','2020-10-22 15:22:03',NULL,'What to expect:\r\n\r\nCOVID-19 safety protocol will be followed; please be prepared with masks and observe social distancing. Temperatures will be taken upon arrival. \r\n\r\nWe will be stationed on the ocean/leeward side of Catalina Island at the Two Harbors campground. In October our temperatures are mild with mid to upper 70’s as the high and upper 50’s to low 60’s for the low. You should use Avalon, CA for your weather apps.\r\n\r\nUse this link to make your boat reservations with Catalina Express https://catalinaexpress.com/schedule-fares.html please select Avalon as the port of arrival. The commute time to Avalon from Long Beach is roughly 70 minutes, you should choose a departure time no later than 9:50 AM on October 19th to ensure that you will arrive before the second leg of the trip. We suggest your return trip is scheduled for the later afternoon/evening of October 22nd. Parking at the Catalina Express Landing is $19 per day, you may consider a driving service to avoid these fees. There is also the option of flying to Catalina via helicopter, this is a shorter commute but the cost is greater, more info available at https://iexhelicopters.com/catalina-island#fly-to-catalina. From Avalon you will take the CYCLONE to Two Harbors - the fee for the CYCLONE is included with your registration cost. \r\n\r\n* More information on meeting time and place for the departure from Avalon to Two Harbors will be provided soon.\r\n\r\nOur cabins max occupancy will be 4 men, feel free to bring your own tent if you prefer as there will be plenty of space with beautiful views of the ocean.\r\n\r\nThere are 3 outdoor showers at the campground free of charge, additional showers are available in the village of Two Harbors which is roughly a 10 min hike from our campsite and costs $2 per 3 minutes.\r\n\r\nInternet access will not be available during the retreat. Laptops, electronic notepads, and camera use ARE NOT permitted during the teaching sessions as it is our desire to minimize all distractions during that time. There is also no available power source for charging such devices.\r\n\r\nAlthough adventure and recreation will be available, much of the time will be devoted to personal reflection on what God is revealing throughout the week. \r\n\r\nThere are activities available for an additional cost such as: snorkeling (free if you have your own equipment), disc golf (free if you have your own discs), kayaking, mountain biking (you may bring your own bike and pay the $7 transportation fee for the Catalina Express - HELMETS REQUIRED) bike rentals are available, spear fishing (you must bring your own equipment), fishing (you must have your own rod/tackle - bait is available)\r\n\r\nFree activities that are offered: rest, ladder golf, spike ball, corn hole, horseshoes, hiking, swimming.\r\n\r\nThe emergency contact person for your loved ones while you are in Two Harbors is Andrew Hobbs, you can reach him at (727) 415-1670. Andrew is also your contact person for questions regarding the retreat. The daytime phone number for Two Harbors Visitors Center is (310) 510-4205 or (310) 510-4211.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat to bring:\r\ncasual/comfortable attire- bring clothing layers\r\nwarm sweater/sweatshirt\r\nwaterproof jacket\r\nhat\r\nbathing suit\r\ncomfortable shoes\r\nsleeping bag\r\npillow\r\ntowel(s) \r\ntoiletries (supplies for shower are not provided)\r\nsunscreen\r\nreusable water bottle\r\njournal\r\npen/pencil\r\nBible\r\nadditional money for rental equipment, shopping\r\nflashlight/headlamp\r\n\r\nIt is very dark at night with uneven ground. This is a beautiful but rustic setting, the above list is for reference but please bring any other items you feel necessary to have for these conditions. \r\n\r\nWater, coffee and beverages are provided. Please let us know of any medical diet needs.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis event is not to be missed! Registration will cut off at 30 men, please register early! In effort to prepare appropriately for food and supplies we ask you to please register by October 12th (one week prior to the event) however we will leave registration open until October 16th for your convenience.\r\n\r\n*A limited amount of partial or full scholarships are available as needed on a first come first served basis. Please contact Andrew to discuss your needs.',15484,429421,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5246\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Catalina Island, Two Harbors Campground\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"90704\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"33.440189\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-118.491782\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"California\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-catalina-island-two-harbors-campground-ca-us-andrew-hobbs',NULL,'2020-09-30 06:09:50','2024-04-10 15:22:03'),
	('9bc65c2e-e302-42ca-b296-57900d5d5a1a',2,2014,'WAH BASIC - Changhua City, CH, TW | Samuel Livingston',NULL,'weekly',' No. 40, Alley 1, Lane 2, Dabu Road','CH',NULL,'Changhua City','500','TW',120.5523770,24.0492720,'Chang-hua',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:03',0,'men','2020-10-19 15:22:04','2020-10-22 15:22:04',NULL,'Do you find it hard to be spiritually fed at your church or small group? Would you like to go deeper as a man into your “adventure to live, your beauty to rescue, and the battle you must fight?” As major themes of Wild at Heart BASIC you will discover new answers and questions for your journey.  Come join us, the men of Taiwan Missionary Fellowship October 19-22 in Changhua at the Manresa Center seeking the story we were meant to live. \r\n\r\n    Built into the BASIC retreat schedule are “covenants of silence” so men have dedicated time to hear from God, journal, and go deeper into the issues raised in the teachings.  BASIC Wild at Heart Boot Camp is for men ready to enter a time of soul-searching and fellowship. We are setting the table for you to find like-hearted men who can walk with you in your masculine spiritual journey.  \r\n\r\nThe typical attendee is a TMF male, but we welcome any interested man 20 years of age &amp; older not needing translation from English. Non-Christians may feel comfortable attending as well. \r\n\r\n Retreat fee covers all lodging, meals, and bedding. Cost is $3500 TWD if registered before September 20, if registered later, cost is $4000 TWD. Registration closes on September 30. BASIC begins with dinner Monday October 19 and concludes with lunch on Thursday at noon. Please register online (https://tinyurl.com/TaiwanWild) for the retreat orientation and the BASIC Wild at Heart Boot Camp.',15167,125072,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4949\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\" No. 40, Alley 1, Lane 2, Dabu Road\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Changhua City\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"CH\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"500\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"tw\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"24.049272\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"120.552377\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Chang-hua\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"Taiwan\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-changhua-city-ch-tw-samuel-livingston',NULL,'2020-06-10 04:06:37','2024-04-10 15:22:04'),
