	('9bc65c2f-e7be-48f8-ad7c-cec9b3958e09',2,1973,'WAH BASIC - Clinton, AR, AR, US | Guy Lester',NULL,'weekly','4772 Highway 110','AR',NULL,'Clinton, AR','72031','US',-92.4605280,35.7218690,'Arkansas',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:04',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:04','2020-10-04 15:22:04',NULL,'Cost is $125 per man, to cover 3 nights lodging, and 8 meals (includes dinner Thursday, and breakfast Sunday).\r\n\r\nWe also recommend bringing hiking boots.\r\n\r\nWe would appreciate completing registration by September 24, 2020.\r\n\r\nYou may also contact Guy Lester at 501-654-4434, or lesterj2415@yahoo.com, for more information.',15137,311178,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4923\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"4772 Highway 110\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Clinton, AR\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"AR\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"72031\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"35.721869\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-92.460528\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Arkansas\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-clinton-ar-ar-us-guy-lester-0',NULL,'2020-05-30 07:05:43','2024-04-10 15:22:04'),
	('9bc65c30-0434-46aa-bf0e-09a20235ad1e',2,1897,'WAH BASIC - Lowesville, VA, US | Kenny Longo',NULL,'weekly','','VA',NULL,'Lowesville','22967','US',-79.0647490,37.7190280,'Virginia',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:04',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:04','2020-10-04 15:22:04',NULL,'Cost for the entire retreat is $200.00.   Includes all meals prepared on site. Attendee will need to byo bed linens or sleeping bag, and pillow. Rooms are bunk style with mattress. \r\nWe\'ll be staying at CrossRoads Camp and Conference Center nestled in the Virginia Blue Ridge. It\'s the perfect setting for the BASIC retreat.\r\nThis event will be limited to the first 30 attendees.  Participants must be 18 or older.  Social distancing protocol will be observed.\r\nClick on this link to register https://graceefc.net/basic',14107,52146,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4130\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lowesville\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"VA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"22967\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"37.719028\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-79.064749\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Virginia\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-lowesville-va-us-kenny-longo',NULL,'2019-08-22 11:08:22','2024-04-10 15:22:04'),
	('9bc65c30-2050-44db-b2da-2e0b18f2af2c',3,2016,'CORE - Cascade, ID, US | Lesley Herzog',NULL,'weekly','1410 Depot Way','ID',NULL,'Cascade','83611','US',-116.0177070,44.4935250,'Idaho',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:04',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:04','2020-10-04 15:22:04',NULL,'Nights and mornings in the mountains can be chilly this time of year (we are at 4800 ft elevation). We will encourage going outdoors for Response times. Bring layers and warm clothing. You will also need your own bedding &amp; towels.',15289,244574,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5055\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"1410 Depot Way\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Cascade\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"ID\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"83611\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"44.493525\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-116.017707\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Idaho\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-cascade-id-us-lesley-herzog',NULL,'2020-07-16 01:07:32','2024-04-10 15:22:04'),
	('9bc65c30-3cdd-461d-9ae1-509c3c8c8a51',3,1887,'CORE - Lowesville, VA, US | Cheryl Haymes',NULL,'weekly','2247 Little Piney RD','VA',NULL,'Lowesville','22967','US',-79.1381160,37.7660720,'Virginia',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:04',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:04','2020-10-04 15:22:04',NULL,'The CORE Event is to be held in the beautiful Blue Ridge Mountains. The leaves should be changing and the scenery breathtaking. You should bring season appropriate comfortable clothing and comfortable walking/hiking shoes. There will be time to spend alone with your Father and opportunity to revel in His creation through hiking, sitting by the stream, or rocking in the rocking chairs at the dining hall. For the more adventurous, you may choose to rock climb or to do the high ropes course and zip line for a small fee. \r\n\r\nThe size of the event is limited to 25 so please sign up soon.',14929,414494,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4763\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"2247 Little Piney RD\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lowesville\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"VA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"22967\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"37.766072\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-79.138116\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Virginia\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-lowesville-va-us-cheryl-haymes',NULL,'2020-03-15 12:03:16','2024-04-10 15:22:04'),
	('9bc65c30-59a1-4f83-bd5d-1bb6fb2909c4',3,1500,'CORE - Sand Springs, OK, US | Amy Thomas',NULL,'weekly','1651 Old North Rd','OK',NULL,'Sand Springs','74063','US',-96.0851720,36.1579870,'Oklahoma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:04',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:05','2020-10-04 15:22:05',NULL,'Join us for an unforgettable weekend at Canyon Crossing Conference and Retreat Center, just minutes from downtown Tulsa, Oklahoma.',14775,404144,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4708\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"1651 Old North Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Sand Springs\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"OK\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"74063\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"36.157987\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-96.085172\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Oklahoma\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-sand-springs-ok-us-amy-thomas-0',NULL,'2020-02-25 08:02:17','2024-04-10 15:22:05'),
	('9bc65c30-78f4-4b57-a311-acf549797c94',2,1610,'WAH BASIC - Spring City, PA, US | Larry Si',NULL,'weekly','68 Bertolet School Road','PA',NULL,'Spring City','19475','US',-75.6518800,40.1584000,'Pennsylvania',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:05',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:05','2020-10-04 15:22:05',NULL,'',15326,17968,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5089\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"68 Bertolet School Road\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Spring City\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"PA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"19475\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"40.158400\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-75.651880\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Pennsylvania\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-spring-city-pa-us-larry-si-1',NULL,'2020-08-03 06:08:47','2024-04-10 15:22:05'),
	('9bc65c30-95e4-452e-ab28-4aaf83b5785f',2,2017,'WAH BASIC - Denton, TX, US | Stuart Brown',NULL,'weekly','8200 E Mckinney St.','TX',NULL,'Denton','76208','US',-97.0374370,33.1847150,'Texas',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:05',0,'men','2020-10-01 15:22:05','2020-10-04 15:22:05',NULL,'Wild at Heart BASIC Boot Camp - Oct 1-4, 2020\r\n\r\nCamp Copass\r\n8200 E. McKinney Street\r\nDenton,  TX 76208\r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nAll the information you need prior to arrival at this event is included below.\r\n\r\nThis page last updated Jan 20, 2020\r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nPLEASE USE THE LINK IN THE TUITION SECTION BELOW TO REGISTER AND PAY FOR THE EVENT.\r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nEvent Description\r\n\r\nWild at Heart BASIC is not just another men’s retreat.  That’s the last thing any man needs.  The reason most messages for men ultimately fail is simple:  they ignore what is deep and true to a man’s heart and try to shape him up through pressure and various forms of compliance.\r\n\r\nNot this retreat!  This weekend is an honest trek into the deep passions and desires of a man’s heart, into the healing of the wounds he’s taken in this battle, into the realm of fatherhood, sex, and calling - life as it was meant to be lived.  Through the video sessions, the times of quiet reflection, the movies, the adventures and the downtime, you will discover something profound about the heart of God and the heart he gave you as a man.  Those who have been, say it is one of the greatest weekends of their entire life. \r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nAudience\r\n\r\n\r\nDue to the intimate and personal nature of the content, Wild at Heart BASIC cannot be viewed as a father/son event initially.  We strongly encourage fathers and sons to attend, but they will need to participate in different Boot Camps, at least for each of their first experiences of this Boot Camp.  \r\n\r\nDue to the nature and depth of the content and experience, Wild at Heart Basic Boot Camp is not designed for youth.  You must be at least 18 years of age by the date of the event to attend.\r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nTuition\r\n\r\n\r\nTuition for this event is $295.  This covers the cost of lodging (hotel style rooms), all meals (Thursday dinner through Sunday breakfast), video teaching and event supplies.  No transportation is provided to or from the event.\r\n\r\nThere are two payment options:\r\n\r\nPay the full amount of $295, which includes a $100 non-refundable deposit.\r\n\r\nPay the non-refundable deposit of $100, then pay the remaining amount of $195 before Sept 1, 2020, three weeks prior to the event.  Accounts not paid in full by Sept. 1, 2020, will be automatically charged the outstanding balance on Sept.  1, 2020.\r\n\r\nPlease click on this link to register and pay for the Wild at Heart BASIC Boot Camp:\r\n\r\nhttps://dfwallies.regfox.com/wild-at-heart-basic\r\n\r\nNote: We have 18 rooms for 36 attendees.  Reservations will be on a first come first served basis.  If this Boot Camp is full, please consider registering for the April, 2021 Wild at Heart Basic Boot Camp to be held at the same location.  We will keep a small waiting list, in case there are cancellations.\r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nSchedule and Content\r\n\r\n\r\nCheck in is Thursday evening 4:30-6:30\r\n\r\nDinner is at 7 pm, followed by the 1st video session.  You DO NOT want to miss the Thursday evening session as it sets the tone and pace for the entire weekend experience.\r\n\r\nCheck out is Sunday at 12:00pm.  Lunch Sunday is not included.\r\n\r\nWild at Heart BASIC is a Wild at Heart Boot Camp led by John Eldredge and his team through eleven video sessions.  \r\n\r\nPhones, laptops, notebooks and cameras are NOT permitted during the sessions.  Our desire is to minimize all distractions during the sessions.\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nCamp Information\r\n\r\n\r\nDirections to Camp Copass can be found here:\r\n\r\nhttps://campcopass.com/contact-us/driving-directions/\r\n\r\nWe will be staying in the Tally Retreat Center.  All rooms are double occupancy,  2 queen beds, full sized bathroom and coffee bar.  All linens are provided, and there is an elevator.  Our video sessions will be in a conference room, on the same floor as our rooms.  More information on the rooms can be found here:\r\n\r\nhttps://campcopass.com/facilities/accomodations/tally-retreat-center/\r\n\r\nThe menu for all the meals is provided here:\r\n\r\nhttps://campcopass.com/retreats/dining-hall-menu/\r\n\r\nRemember Thursday dinner through Sunday breakfast is included in your tuition.  If you have any special needs, please note on your registration at sign up.  You can also email Stu Brown at stu2fly1@yahoo.com, no later than Sept. 1, 2020.  Please note that special needs refers to medical conditions and medically restricted diets.  We are not able to accommodate special preferences.  \r\n\r\nCamp Copass is located on the shores of Lake Lewisville, which is a beautiful spot to hike, fish (shore only, bring your own gear), play basketball, horseshoes, softball, volleyball, frisbee or miniature golf.  There will also be a guided fishing trip (limited space) on Saturday afternoon, for an additional fee.  A Camp map can be found here:\r\n\r\nhttps://campcopass.com/the-camp/camp-map/\r\n\r\nAlthough there are lots of recreational opportunities, You will also want to spend time in personal reflection as you consider what God is revealing throughout the weekend.  We will not be the only event taking place at the camp so some areas may be unavailable.\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nAttire\r\n\r\nBoot camp is comfortable casual.  Bring season appropriate clothes, a waterproof jacket, hat and comfortable shoes.  Walking is required between the Tally Retreat Center and the dining hall.\r\n\r\n————————————————————————\r\n\r\nEmergency Contact Information\r\n\r\nWe strongly encourage all participants to “unplug” from the steady stream of noise and demands that is constantly bombarding us through our cell phones and other devices.  Our desire is for you to be completely “present” and relaxed throughout the weekend; able to hear from God and others.  Please provide your family with the emergency phone numbers below and let them know that you will be unavailable from 7:00pm Thursday until 12:00 pm on Sunday after the close of Boot Camp.  \r\n\r\nStu Brown\r\n(972) 365-6354 (leave message if no answer)\r\n\r\nOnly use the Camp Copass phone number is you are unable to reach the emergency contact. \r\n\r\nCamp Copass Office\r\n(940) 565-0050',13676,411346,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"3745\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"8200 E Mckinney St.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Denton\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"TX\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"76208\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"33.184715\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-97.037437\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Texas\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-denton-tx-us-stuart-brown',NULL,'2019-03-16 11:03:37','2024-04-10 15:22:05'),
