	('9bc65c33-bc22-4c74-a3a6-271eb5688fb7',2,1949,'WAH BASIC - Peshastin, WA, US | Joshua Pendleton',NULL,'weekly','Camas Creek Rd','WA',NULL,'Peshastin','98847','US',-120.5820500,47.4772690,'Washington',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:07',0,'men','2020-08-13 15:22:07','2020-08-16 15:22:07',NULL,'',15343,427861,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"5109\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"Camas Creek Rd\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Peshastin\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"WA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"98847\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"47.477269\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-120.582050\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Washington\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-peshastin-wa-us-joshua-pendleton',NULL,'2020-08-09 11:08:19','2024-04-10 15:22:07'),
	('9bc65c33-d952-4fce-a6fb-e9b5d80299cd',2,2031,'WAH BASIC - New Freedom, PA, US | Jay Ashworth',NULL,'weekly','8 Lennon Lane','PA',NULL,'New Freedom','17349','US',-76.6717940,39.7448540,'Pennsylvania',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:07',0,'men','2020-08-13 15:22:07','2020-08-16 15:22:07',NULL,'',15177,198815,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4964\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"8 Lennon Lane\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"8 Lennon Lane\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"New Freedom\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"PA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"17349\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"39.744854\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-76.671794\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Pennsylvania\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-new-freedom-pa-us-jay-ashworth',NULL,'2020-06-12 07:06:56','2024-04-10 15:22:07'),
	('9bc65c33-f791-4e5c-8bd6-8074cc6207c8',2,635,'WAH BASIC - Lakewood, WI, US | Chad Hendricks',NULL,'weekly','18495 PEEK RD','WI',NULL,'Lakewood','54138','US',-88.3904800,45.3449970,'Wisconsin',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:07',0,'men','2020-08-13 15:22:07','2020-08-16 15:22:07',NULL,'Location:\r\n\r\nOur location is an old 80 acre family farm in Lakewood, WI. This land is surrounded by the Nicolet National Forest. We will be camping outside with no running water or electricity. It will be an amazing experience of unplugging from the modern world.\r\n\r\nStart Time:\r\n\r\nNoon to 6pm is your time to set up camp. Dinner will start at 6pm on Thursday with our first session following.\r\n\r\nWhat Should I bring:\r\n\r\nBring a notebook/journal and pens. Camping gear. If you need something, just ask.\r\n\r\nAccommodations:\r\n\r\nBring your own tents, campers and gear. If you don\'t own any of these items, please let me know and we will find what you need.\r\n\r\nRegistration Fee:\r\n\r\nThe fees for this event is to help pay for fresh water, gasoline for the generator, snacks, toilet paper, etc.\r\n\r\nThere is an option to buy the meal plan option. We will be having a local restaurant cater to us.\r\n\r\nAirports:\r\n\r\nClosest airport is Austin Straubel in Green Bay, WI. (1.5 hours drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nGeneral Mitchell in Milwaukee, WI (3 hr 15 min drive to Lakewood)\r\n\r\nOther Activities:\r\n\r\nThere is free time each day. Currently, we will be offering map and compass (orienteering) training and archery training as added activities.\r\n\r\nFOOD:\r\n\r\nYou can bring your own food, but you can also purchase food with the group. If you bring food, plan on keeping preparation time to a minimum. (I recommend bringing some snacks and letting the food prep to the professionals.) Food orders will be collected before the event via email and payment will be made when you register. The menu for this trip is below.\r\n\r\nTotal Food Costs: $105.00 plus $20 for tip\r\n\r\nBreakfast @ $10 each (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)\r\n\r\n1. Scrambled Eggs, Sausage, Tator tots, English muffin, Danish\r\n2. Ham &amp; Egg on an English muffin, hashbrowns, yogurt, mixed fruit\r\n3. Pancakes &amp; Syrup, sausage links, American fries, apple,\r\n\r\nLunch @ $10 each (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)\r\n1. Chicken Bacon Wrap, granola bar, chips\r\n2. sub sandwich, cookie, chips\r\n3. Burger with potato wedges\r\n\r\nDinner @ $15 each (Thursday, Friday, Saturday)\r\n1. 3 piece Broasted chicken, mashed potatoes, dressing, Green Beans, Pasta Salad\r\n2. 1/2 Rack BBQ ribs, baked potato, dinner roll, side salad\r\n3. Fish Fry (Friday) Breaded Alaskan Pollack , baby reds, coleslaw, rye bread',14227,411000,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4155\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"18495 PEEK RD\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lakewood\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"WI\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"54138\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"45.344997\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-88.390480\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Wisconsin\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-lakewood-wi-us-chad-hendricks-0',NULL,'2019-08-29 09:08:52','2024-04-10 15:22:07'),
	('9bc65c34-16c7-405a-be75-401555195baf',2,1018,'WAH BASIC - Keystone, SD, US | Carey Warren',NULL,'weekly','24631 Iron Mountain Road','SD',NULL,'Keystone','57751','US',-103.4268950,43.8972580,'South Dakota',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:07',0,'men','2020-08-09 15:22:07','2020-08-12 15:22:07',NULL,'This is the W@H Basic for Bikers, set in the Heart of Everything that Is - the Black Hills of South Dakota - during the 80th Rally. Cabin 19 of Spokane Creek campground is reserved, if you’re riding in. Just let me know you’re coming! If you’re bringing your RV, you can reserve your spot at www.spokanecreekresort.com.\r\n\r\nWe stand at twilight of the third age with The Wave rising round about us. Stands up, guys. Ride to Live!',14445,409381,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4403\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"24631 Iron Mountain Road\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Keystone\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"SD\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"57751\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"43.897258\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-103.426895\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"South Dakota\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-keystone-sd-us-carey-warren-0',NULL,'2019-11-28 03:11:11','2024-04-10 15:22:07'),
	('9bc65c34-35fc-4c2a-a041-d2eb302ceeab',2,1649,'WAH BASIC - Suches, GA, US | Jake Dowling',NULL,'weekly','853 Camp Rd.','GA',NULL,'Suches','30572','US',-84.0500560,34.7287230,'Georgia',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:07',0,'men','2020-08-06 15:22:07','2020-08-09 15:22:07',NULL,'Prepare to spend 3.5 days unplugged from the grind and pace of life to reconnect with your Father and receive this life-giving message.  There will be plenty of time for rest, reflection, adventure, and fellowship at the beautiful Mountain Fellowship Camp located in the North Georgia mountains in Suches, GA.  (853 Camp Road, Suches GA 30572)\r\n\r\nTotal Cost: $150 (includes lodging and meals)\r\n[$50 deposit by July 10, full payment by July 31]\r\n\r\nArrival: 4:00-5:00 pm on Thursday, August 6\r\nEvent Concludes: 11:45 am on Sunday, August 9\r\n\r\nOPTIONAL: Sunday afternoon kayaking trip down the Chattahoochee River, 1:00-5:00 (located at Wildwood Outfitters in Cleveland, GA, approximately 1 hour from camp).  Cost is $35 (pay upon arrival Sunday afternoon).\r\n\r\nOther Info:  You will have some free time on Friday and Saturday afternoons where you can swim, canoe, paddle board, go fishing, hiking, etc., or spend alone time with God.\r\n\r\nNote: There is no cell phone signal at camp.  We will provide you with an emergency contact number and there is a land line available in case of emergencies.  Once you drive through Suches you will likely lose cell service.  See below for detailed driving directions once you pass through Suches.\r\n\r\nDirections from Suches, GA: Go north on hwy 60 approx 7 miles. Turn right on Grizzle Creek Rd. (Wildcat store and a fire station are located at this intersection). Take Grizzle Creek about ½ mile to stop sign. Turn left on Johnny Gap Road. Go about 100 yards and turn right onto Camp Road – there is a sign here for Mountain Fellowship Camp. Go through green gate and continue about ½ mile to Lodge.',15154,419062,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4941\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"853 Camp Rd.\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Suches\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"GA\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"30572\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"34.728723\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-84.050056\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Georgia\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/wah-basic-suches-ga-us-jake-dowling',NULL,'2020-06-04 08:06:30','2024-04-10 15:22:07'),
	('9bc65c34-5572-4855-9aa4-f64ff54a69d3',3,1982,'CORE - St.George, UT, US | Carol Huebner',NULL,'weekly','920 W Tonaquint Dr','UT',NULL,'St.George','84770','US',-113.6038260,37.0730530,'Utah',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'2024-04-10 15:22:07',0,'men','2020-08-03 15:22:07','2020-08-06 15:22:07',NULL,'Bring lunch. Refrigerator and microwave available.',15209,426746,'\"{\\\"lid\\\":\\\"4996\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"street\\\":\\\"920 W Tonaquint Dr\\\",\\\"additional\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"St.George\\\",\\\"province\\\":\\\"UT\\\",\\\"postal_code\\\":\\\"84770\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":\\\"37.073053\\\",\\\"longitude\\\":\\\"-113.603826\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"3\\\",\\\"is_primary\\\":\\\"0\\\",\\\"province_name\\\":\\\"Utah\\\",\\\"country_name\\\":\\\"United States\\\"}\"','/core-stgeorge-ut-us-carol-huebner-0',NULL,'2020-06-24 07:06:45','2024-04-10 15:22:07'),
